{title: Praise to the Lord, the Almighty}
{artist: Joachim Neander (1650-1680); tr. Catherine Winkworth (1827-1878)}
{key: F}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[F]Praise to the [C]Lord, the Al[Dm]mighty, the [Bb]King of cre[C]ation!
[F]O my soul, [C]praise Him, for [Dm]He is thy [Bb]health and sal[C]vation!
[Bb]All ye who [F]hear, now to His [C]temple draw near;
[Bb]Praise Him in [C]glad ado[F]ration!
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[F]Praise to the [C]Lord, who o’er [Dm]all things so [Bb]wondrously [C]reigneth,
[F]Shelters thee [C]under His [Dm]wings, yea, so [Bb]gently sus[C]taineth!
[Bb]Hast thou not [F]seen how thy de[C]sires e’er have been
[Bb]Granted in [C]what He or[F]daineth?
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[F]Praise to the [C]Lord, who doth [Dm]prosper thy [Bb]work and de[C]fend thee!
[F]Surely His [C]goodness and [Dm]mercy here [Bb]daily at[C]tend thee.
[Bb]Ponder a[F]new what the Al[C]mighty can do,
[Bb]If with His [C]love He be[F]friend thee.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[F]Praise to the [C]Lord! O let [Dm]all that is [Bb]in me a[C]dore Him!
[F]All that hath [C]life and breath, [Dm]come now with [Bb]praises be[C]fore Him!
[Bb]Let the A[F]men sound from His [C]people again:
[Bb]Gladly for [C]aye we a[F]dore Him.
{eov}
